[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2451731096","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98707#issuecomment-2451731096","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98707","id":2451731096,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SInKY","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-01T11:32:29Z","updated_at":"2024-11-01T11:32:29Z","body":"Await is not supported in methods called from the engine like this, see:\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/88139\r\n\r\nNote that `await` doesn't stop execution, it releases execution back to the caller and then resumes after the signal is fired","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2451731096/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2452038377","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98707#issuecomment-2452038377","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98707","id":2452038377,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SJyLp","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-01T15:09:37Z","updated_at":"2024-11-01T15:09:37Z","body":"I suppose the only workaround is to customize resources to a temp folder beforehand and just load them at the hooks.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2452038377/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2459024532","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98707#issuecomment-2459024532","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98707","id":2459024532,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SkbyU","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-06T08:47:10Z","updated_at":"2024-11-06T08:51:27Z","body":"Note that even GDScript code is not \"`await`-aware\" by default. The following code will print 2, then 1, because calling an asynchronous function without `await` does not wait for the coroutine to complete.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc async_func():\r\n    await get_tree().process_frame\r\n    print(1)\r\n\r\nfunc _ready():\r\n    async_func()\r\n    print(2)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAll core APIs are synchronous, all methods execute immediately[^1], coroutines do not exist for the core. Similarly, when the core calls any GDScript function (virtual methods, `filter()`/`map()`/`reduce()` callables, etc.), the core expects the function to be synchronous.\r\n\r\nWe should clarify this in the GDScript documentation. But I doubt we can do more for `void` methods[^2]. In theory we could add a static analyzer warning and/or debug runtime validation (coroutines return an `GDScriptFunctionState` instance), but using `await` in a native virtual method may be valid, so the warning would be a false positive.\r\n\r\n[^1]: However, the effect of the method can be asynchronous, for example `call_deferred()` adds a call to the message queue, and the call itself will be made later. Same with `Tween`.\r\n[^2]: For non-`void` methods, we should probably check the return type instead of an implicit conversion.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2459024532/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]